From 64c1274878481ad383ffdb34ab843b48219a320a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mesh-LLM CI <ci@mesh-llm.local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:25:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mesh: record why a reserve guard on a missing stage program
 was rejected

sched_reserve reserves the graph selected by active_stage_program(). With a program
present the builder emits only the staged layer range; with none it emits every
layer, and graph_reserve then allocates real buffers for all of them. That
un-sliced reserve is what froze the host while layers [0,2) were being diagnosed.

Refusing the reserve whenever a stage plan has no program looked like the obvious
fix. It is wrong. The first reserve of a stage-plan runtime happens while the
context is being created, and the program is extracted afterwards, so a null
program is the normal state at that point rather than an error. The guard rejected
every range and every run of the synthetic tiny model with "stage plan runtime has
no stage program; refusing to reserve the whole-model graph", so it is removed and
this note replaces it, to save the next person the attempt.

What established this is tools/v41-mktiny.cpp: a synthetic deepseek41 model at toy
dimensions that exercises the same loader, graph builder and stage-program
extraction in seconds and for a few hundred kilobytes. It showed six reserves on a
null program followed by a successful context creation -- something no full-size
experiment could have shown without risking the machine again.
---
 src/llama-context.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/llama-context.cpp b/src/llama-context.cpp
index 686f0ab..4052cd0 100644
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -712,6 +712,12 @@ void llama_context::sched_reserve(const skippy_graph_build_inputs & graph_build_
             program->program.computation_generation != computation_generation) {
         throw std::runtime_error("stage program computation configuration changed after installation");
     }
+    // NOTE: a guard refusing the reserve whenever a stage plan has no program was tried here and
+    // removed. It is not a legitimate state to test for: the first reserve of a stage-plan runtime
+    // happens while the context is being created and the program is extracted afterwards, so
+    // active_stage_program() is legitimately null at that point. The synthetic tiny model in
+    // tools/v41-mktiny.cpp shows this in seconds -- every one of its six reserves runs with a null
+    // program, and the runtime still opens once its stage program installs.
     if (!sched_need_reserve) {
         return;
     }
